            <ArticleTitle>Respiratory pathogen panels in the hospital: good or unnecessary?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>226-230</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/QCO.0000000000000357</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE OF REVIEW" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">We aim to review the epidemiology of respiratory viral infections and the strengths and limitations of multiplex respiratory pathogen panels that are currently available along with their respective features and differences.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RECENT FINDINGS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">We give particular emphasis to the pathogens included on each test and evaluate their performance in the hospital setting.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SUMMARY" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">We conclude with a discussion on the evidence for the clinical utility of respiratory pathogen multiplex panels in hospitalized patients, including the potential for coinfection with viral and bacterial pathogens.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
